{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2aecfe15c341f5d5","name":"Pirate","source":{"id":"source:reference-2aecfe15c341f5d5","title":"Pirate","revision":18992,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:06:02Z","sha256":"3b3b6b31a05a8d396442ddad7555de668f915522d53582934fbd68ae1ef7627b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18992","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Pirate&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2aecfe15c341f5d5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Pirate moniker can be applied to just about anyone who makes a living robbing and stealing ships. From bloodthirsty crews lurking on the fringes of space, to professional thieves plying the trade lanes, Pirates are an age-old problem in the galaxy and one not likely to go away anytime soon. Generally, Pirates are little better than bandits, lying in wait to beset a passing ship.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["However, not all Pirates fit the cruel image attributed to most of their kind. Many follow a strict code of conduct, being more selective about whom they hit, how often, and when. Some Pirates never kill, while others strike only at ships loyal to the Empire. It can be difficult, however, to figure out what sort of Pirate is about to be encountered, and sometimes it's better to shoot first and sort out the details later.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Pirate Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6/",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," 2/",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316